From d040a4bc9aeb045f84477541cbebdbd24ce7c130 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ephico2real2 <ephico2real@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 07:01:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ztunnel: fail-closed HBONE-only admission and native
 Kubernetes node names

Datapath (review findings 1-5 on the C1 draft):
- Add a sticky load-time ztunnel_required obligation. A Required program never
  forwards as an ordinary endpoint: a missing, foreign (wrong lxc_id) or
  partial-family own cilium_lxc entry is quarantined.
- HBONE-only mode accepts only the TCP/15008 transport shape in both
  directions. Remove the world/CIDR/reserved, DNS and host plaintext
  exceptions. Check REPLY packets on actual packet ports so an older plaintext
  conntrack entry cannot carry data after release. Native policy on the outer
  15008 flow is not widened. TCP/15008 is not authentication; ztunnel supplies
  the cryptographic proof.
- Kubelet probes to released Required endpoints are an explicit open gate: the
  slim Pod type has no probe ports, so no host exception is provided.

xDS:
- Publish Workload.Node as the Kubernetes Node name from Cilium's native node
  table (local-cluster rows only, every address, no NodeIP fallback). Reject
  missing, ambiguous, unsynchronized or foreign-cluster bindings. Bind once at
  the Address response boundary and close the stream when a published binding
  changes without an endpoint event.
- Set the ztunnel NODE_NAME to spec.nodeName to match.

Tests: race on pkg/endpoint, pkg/maps/lxcmap, pkg/datapath/config and
pkg/ztunnel/xds (120 top-level / 345 total pass, 21 pre-existing
integration-dependent skips), vet, dpgen drift check, BPF build_all, and
privileged BPF PROG_RUN (63 subtests, including 26 new admission cases).
Live: the native node tables on cmtc-a/cmtc-b resolve all 35 CiliumEndpoints
to the API Pod spec.nodeName. Not a release; the ClusterMesh/ztunnel guard
stays closed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
